WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.610
- [Tutor] A Pap test

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.910
is a test to screen for cervical cancer

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.563
or other cervical diseases.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.550
Your cervix is the
lower part of the uterus

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.173
at the top of your vagina.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.060
A Pap test is used to check
your cervix for abnormal cells.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.140
Abnormal cells can sometimes
turn into cervical cancer

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.403
if they aren't treated.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.463
A Pap test can be part of a pelvic exam.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.340
First, your healthcare provider

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.693
will place an instrument called
a speculum into your vagina.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.360
The speculum will be opened

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.293
so that your cervix can be seen.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.170
Next, your provider will
use a scraper or brush

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.483
to gently collect cells from your cervix.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.060
Your cells will be examined
at a lab under a microscope

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.963
to see if any of them are abnormal.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:04.850
It usually takes about one to three weeks

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.193
to get your test results.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.190
If you have questions about this test

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.730
or your test results,

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:13.973
talk to your provider.

